=== PARITY (vs web TriggerConfigurator.tsx) ===
  Data -> the web component is a CONTROLLED form (`trigger` prop + `onChange`) with ONE data hook,
    `useGeofences()`. Native parity binds the editable trigger through a P1/S8 state holder
    (TriggerConfiguratorModel) that owns it and re-emits every edit via `onChange` (the web callback), and
    binds the geofence query through the `GeofenceSource` seam projected into loading/error/empty/data +
    stale/offline. The view performs NO HTTP.
  Cron -> CronExpression.build / .parse are faithful ports: build = `"${minute} ${hour} * * ${dow}"` with
    dow `*` for 0-or-7 days else comma-joined; parse requires exactly 5 whitespace fields with `*` dom+month
    and integer minute+hour, drops non-integer day tokens (web `.map(Number).filter(!isNaN)`). EXECUTED-green
    incl. a build↔parse round-trip.
  Day toggle -> TriggerAdapter.toggleDay reproduces web handleDayToggle exactly: empty = every day; toggling
    off an empty set selects the other six; membership toggle otherwise; a full seven normalises back to
    empty. EXECUTED-green.
  Signal value -> TriggerAdapter.signalValue is the web signalValueFromInput port (changed→none, bool key→
    value_bool, `state`→value_text, else value_num via a parseFloat-semantics scan + `|| 0`); displayValue is
    the web `value` derivation (bool default true, state default "online", numeric default 20, integers print
    without a `.0` tail). EXECUTED-green.
  Signal edit rules -> setSignal seeds the new signal's type default (bool `=`+true / state `=`+"online" /
    numeric `<`+20), setOperator drops the value for `changed` else re-coerces, setSignalValue re-coerces, and
    the "Fire on any change" toggle flips between `changed` and a re-coerced `=` — each a verbatim port,
    EXECUTED-green.
  Geofence edit rules -> setGeofenceEvent seeds `dwell_minutes ?? 5` for the dwell event and clears it
    (undefined→nil) otherwise (web ternary); the dwell field shows only for the dwell event. EXECUTED-green.
  Schedule mode toggle -> the web ternary `cron_expr: isSimple ? trigger.cron_expr : '0 8 * * *'` is
    reproduced VERBATIM (a simple expression is kept; a non-parseable one resets to the canonical simple
    seed) — including the web's own quirk that the button is a no-op while already simple. Documented, not
    "fixed" (Honesty rule 5).
  States (all render) -> every web branch has a #if DEBUG preview AND the geofence query's
    loading/error/empty/data + stale/offline overlays render (the web maps `geofences ?? []` silently; the
    production native surface surfaces the query states the P4 contract requires — a loading row, an error
    box with retry, a friendly empty caption, and stale/offline chips — never a blank control).
  i18n -> ALL web `t()` keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade (table "TriggerConfigurator"): the 21
    in-component strings (selectGeofence, time, days, cronExpr, cronPlaceholder, cronHint, advancedCron,
    simpleCron, timezone, event, geofence, geofenceEvent, dwellMinutes, dwellHint, signal, operator, value,
    changedOnly, statePlaceholder, common.true/false) + the 4 TRIGGER_TYPES + 9 VEHICLE_EVENTS + 3
    GEOFENCE_EVENTS + 9 SIGNAL_OPERATORS + 9 signal-field labels + 11 timezones + 7 weekday short keys, plus
